---
import CapabilityGrid from '../../components/CapabilityGrid.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectDetailCTA from '../../components/ProjectDetailCTA.astro';
import ProjectDetailHero from '../../components/ProjectDetailHero.astro';
import { beaconCapabilities, beaconProducts, beaconUseCases } from '../../data/beacon';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';

const beacon = projects.find((project) => project.visual === 'beacon');
if (!beacon?.externalHref) throw new Error('Beacon project must have an application URL.');
---

<Layout
  title="Beacon — Conscia Labs"
  description="Beacon is Conscia’s internal AI ecosystem. Beacon Work is the desktop app, Beacon Code the terminal client, and Beacon Cloud supports both."
  noIndex
>
  <div class="project-page">
    <ProjectDetailHero
      name={beacon.name}
      category={beacon.category}
      type={beacon.type}
      description={beacon.description}
      lede="AI help for Conscia colleagues."
      visual={beacon.visual}
      mediaLabel="Beacon Work, Beacon Code, and Beacon Cloud."
      actionLabel="Open Beacon Cloud"
      externalHref={beacon.externalHref}
    />

    <section class="detail-overview section-light" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <div class="container detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">01 / What is Beacon?</p>
          <h2 id="overview-title">Beacon, in three parts.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-overview__copy">
          <p>Beacon is for Conscia colleagues. Use it to make sense of information, work on a document, or tackle an engineering task.</p>
          <p>Work is the desktop app, Code is the terminal client, and Cloud supports both. Work and Code are available for internal Conscia use today, along with the Cloud services they need.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="differentiators section-light" aria-labelledby="ecosystem-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">02 / Available today</p>
            <h2 id="ecosystem-title">Desktop, terminal, and cloud.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Use Work on the desktop or Code in the terminal. Cloud provides the services behind them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="differentiator-grid">
          {beaconProducts.map((product) => (
            <article class="differentiator" style={`--item-accent: ${product.accent}`}>
              <span class="differentiator__number">{product.number}</span>
              <h3>{product.title}</h3>
              <p>{product.description}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CapabilityGrid
      items={beaconCapabilities}
      label="03 / Why Beacon?"
      heading="Help that fits the job."
      introduction="Beacon brings Conscia knowledge and tools into the clients we use for everyday tasks."
    />

    <section class="differentiators section-light" aria-labelledby="use-cases-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">04 / In practice</p>
            <h2 id="use-cases-title">What you can do with it.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>You don’t need to code to use Beacon Work. Start with a document or a question. If you’re doing engineering, Work and Code can help you make changes and check the results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="differentiator-grid">
          {beaconUseCases.map((item) => (
            <article class="differentiator" style={`--item-accent: ${item.accent}`}>
              <span class="differentiator__number">{item.number}</span>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.description}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="detail-overview section-dark" aria-labelledby="autonomy-title">
      <div class="container detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">05 / Planned — not available today</p>
          <h2 id="autonomy-title">Agents that work in the background.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-overview__copy">
          <p>Autonomous Cloud agents and automations aren’t built yet. The plan is for Cloud to run tasks without a desktop or terminal client running.</p>
          <p>An agent could let you know about a new email or calendar invitation. Or it could check something in the background and tell you what needs attention. That’s the direction, not a feature you can use today.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ProjectDetailCTA
      label="06 / Internal Conscia use"
      heading="Try Beacon on your next task."
      description="Work and Code are available to Conscia colleagues, with Cloud supporting both. Open Beacon Cloud at beacon.conscialabs.com to get started."
      actionLabel="Open Beacon Cloud"
      externalHref={beacon.externalHref}
    />
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>
